[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2782682930","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105001#issuecomment-2782682930","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105001","id":2782682930,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6l3F8y","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-07T09:27:57Z","updated_at":"2025-04-07T09:27:57Z","body":"Please describe what the issue is, how it should look and what is wrong with how it looks","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2782682930/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2782935789","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105001#issuecomment-2782935789","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105001","id":2782935789,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6l4Drt","user":{"login":"quqr","id":42091795,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyMDkxNzk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/42091795?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/quqr","html_url":"https://github.com/quqr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/quqr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/quqr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/quqr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/quqr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/quqr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/quqr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/quqr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/quqr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/quqr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-07T11:02:44Z","updated_at":"2025-04-07T11:02:44Z","body":"> Please describe what the issue is, how it should look and what is wrong with how it looks\n\nWhen using a ​​multilayer TileMapLayer​​, a ​​ColorRect​​ with a shader that samples SCREEN_TEXTURE incorrectly samples the screen texture during rendering, causing display anomalies.\n\nAs illustrated in the scenario above:\n\n- There are two ​​TileMapLayers​​.\n\n- Each TileMapLayer has a ​​ColorRect​​ with a shader that samples SCREEN_TEXTURE.\n\n- The first ColorRect correctly samples the screen texture of the ​​first TileMapLayer​​.\n\n- The second ColorRect ​​should sample textures from both the first and second TileMapLayers​​, but instead it ​​only samples the first TileMapLayer's texture​​, ignoring the second layer entirely.\n\n**​​Expected behavior​​:**\nAs shown in the second image, the ColorRect should display textures from ​​both the first and second TileMapLayers​​ (combined screen textures of both layers).\n\n**​​Observed error​​:**\nThe second ColorRect fails to sample the second TileMapLayer's screen texture, resulting in incomplete or incorrect rendering.\n\nWhen multiple ​​ColorRects​​ are present on the **screen**, ​​only one​​ samples textures correctly, while ​​the others exhibit errors​​.\nIf there is only one ColorRect on the **screen**, then it is rendered correctly,\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2782935789/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2782958541","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105001#issuecomment-2782958541","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105001","id":2782958541,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6l4JPN","user":{"login":"kleonc","id":9283098,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODMwOTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9283098?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc","html_url":"https://github.com/kleonc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-07T11:11:53Z","updated_at":"2025-04-07T11:13:22Z","body":"This is correct/intended behavior, the second ColorRect in the MRP uses the same screen texture as the first one, see the docs: [Screen-reading shaders](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/4.4/tutorials/shaders/screen-reading_shaders.html#behind-the-scenes).\n\nAdding a BackBufferCopy draw-wise between the TileMapLayer2 and the second `ColorRect` makes it render as desired:\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7b1eb1fd-deb9-4d01-83b5-5d956d4edbd5)\n\nThis is already documented and not a bug, hence I'm closing this issue. But if you have any suggestions about improving docs further etc. feel free to share them.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2782958541/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]